  "text": {
    "value": "Here’s a concise overview and some workarounds regarding errors and usage for the GitHub Copilot Pull Request Reviewer API (`copilot-pull-request-reviewer`), especially with `gh pr edit`, and interactions with Projects (classic):\n\n### 1. **Requesting Copilot as Reviewer via CLI**\nYou can now assign Copilot to review your pull requests directly from the terminal with the GitHub CLI (v2.88.0+).\n- **Add Copilot as a reviewer:**  \n  ```sh\n  gh pr edit \u003cPR-number\u003e --add-reviewer @copilot\n  ```\n  This is available interactively or non-interactively. You do not need to switch to the browser; Copilot will appear as an option alongside your teammates【3:1†source】.\n\n### 2. **Classic Projects and Copilot Review**\nIf you encounter errors related to Projects (classic), these are usually due to permission mismatches, deprecated APIs, or organizational configuration. Copilot code reviews currently work best with standard repo PR workflows; \"Projects (classic)\" integrations might not always be supported or may throw errors if:\n- You lack the required permissions.\n- Your org/repo has not migrated to the newer Projects experience.\n- The CLI or REST API calls reference unsupported endpoints.\n\n**Workaround:**\n- **Update Permissions:** Ensure you have `write` permissions on the repo.\n- **Use New Projects:** Migrate off Projects (classic) if possible, as GitHub is focusing support on their new Projects system.\n- **Direct REST API Usage:** If “gh pr edit --add-reviewer @copilot” results in errors, try requesting via the REST API:\n  ```sh\n  curl \\\n    -X POST \\\n    -H \"Authorization: ******" \\\n    -H \"Accept: application/vnd.github+json\" \\\n    https://api.github.com/repos/OWNER/REPO/pulls/PR_NUMBER/requested_reviewers \\\n    -d '{\"reviewers\": [\"copilot-pull-request-reviewer[bot]\"]}'\n  ```\n  Replace placeholders with your repo info.\n\n### 3. **Automatic and Manual Copilot Review**\n- **Automatic:** You can configure Copilot to review every PR automatically (or on every push) via repo/org rulesets. This is done in repo settings under **Rulesets** → **Automatically request Copilot code review**.\n- **Manual Re-review:** If Copilot does not re-review on new pushes and you want it to, either turn on the relevant setting or manually trigger via CLI or UI【3:2†source】【3:0†source】.\n\n### 4. **Known Workarounds for Error States**\nIf you encounter a specific error:\n- **“Reviewer not found” or “bot unavailable”**: Ensure Copilot code review is enabled for the repo/org.\n- **Permission Denied**: Double-check your personal and repo access.\n- **Incompatibility with Classic Projects**: Move issues/PRs out of classic projects and into standard workflows or new Projects.\n\n### 5. **Getting Help**\n- **Update CLI**: Make sure you are on the latest GitHub CLI (≥ v2.88.0).\n- **File an Issue:** If errors persist and appear to be bugs, open an issue in the [`cli/cli`](https://github.com/cli/cli/issues) repository with detailed error output.\n\n**References and further reading:**\n- [GitHub Copilot code review docs](https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/github-copilot-on-github/copilot-code-review)\n- [Requesting Copilot reviews with the GitHub CLI](https://github.blog/changelog/2026-03-11-request-copilot-code-review-from-github-cli/)【3:1†source】\n- [Configuring automatic code review by Copilot](https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/github-copilot-on-github/configure-automatic-copilot-code-review)【3:2†source】\n\nIf you share the exact error message, I can provide more targeted troubleshooting steps!",
